From 9bce851bc1ff27af91d336f1fa1e1d8e6b8f3fb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 22:07:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 35/58] perf(server): skip re-hashing already-verified
 downloads

A completed download with an expected hash is re-hashed in full on every
subsequent pull. mbedTLS software SHA-256 runs ~280 MB/s single-threaded,
so a 340 GiB model costs ~20 minutes per pull with zero bytes to
download, and re-registering recipes against a shared checkpoint repeats
the full walk each time.

Record a .verified sidecar (algorithm, digest, size, mtime) after any
successful full verification; a later check whose expected digest and
file facts all match skips the re-hash. Any divergence, a missing or
garbled sidecar, or a failed verification falls back to the full hash,
and failed verification also drops the sidecar. Deleting .verified files
forces full re-verification.

Assisted-by: claude:fable-5
---
 CMakeLists.txt                       |   7 ++
 src/cpp/server/utils/http_client.cpp | 102 ++++++++++++++++-
 test/cpp/test_verify_once.cpp        | 165 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 272 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 test/cpp/test_verify_once.cpp

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index c2d6a5fc2..4afd7118f 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -3999,6 +3999,13 @@ if(BUILD_TESTING AND EXISTS "${_STREAMING_SILENT_STREAM_TEST_SRC}")
     add_cpp_ci_test(StreamingSilentStreamTest CI ON COMMAND test_streaming_silent_stream)
 endif()
 
